The 3-attempt mastery rule
For every problem:
1. Attempt 1: Solve independently for 30–45 minutes.
2. Attempt 2: If stuck, understand the approach, close the solution, and code it yourself.
3. Attempt 3: Re-solve after 2–3 days without looking at your previous code.
4. Revision: Re-solve after 7 days and again after 30 days.
You have mastered a problem when you can explain:
- Why this approach works
- How you derived the solution
- TC and SC
- Edge cases
- How to write the code without looking at notes
Daily schedule (90 minutes)
Time	Activity
15 min	Revise yesterday's problem
45 min	Solve one new problem
20 min	Understand and implement optimal solution
10 min	Write notes: pattern, TC, SC